WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.279
This is the worksheet workbook

00:00:02.279 --> 00:00:04.475
for the On-Chain Operator Program.

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:06.833
In this film you will learn which sheet to

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:09.137
open, when in the course you open it, and

00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:11.385
how a yellow cell becomes a green answer.

00:00:12.685 --> 00:00:15.180
A long course is easy to lose track of.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.097
The decision you do not write down

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:18.985
is the one you cannot review.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.188
This file is where the

00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:21.600
lesson turns into a record.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.128
By the end you will be

00:00:24.128 --> 00:00:25.655
able to do four things.

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:27.700
Open the workbook in a spreadsheet.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.153
Pick the sheet that matches

00:00:29.153 --> 00:00:30.595
the lesson you are on.

00:00:30.595 --> 00:00:31.811
Type in a yellow cell,

00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:33.485
and read the green answer.

00:00:33.485 --> 00:00:35.270
And keep secrets out of every sheet.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.320
Start with the safety line.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.303
The file is educational only, and it will never

00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:43.530
ask for a seed phrase or a key.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.225
Then open the workbook.

00:00:45.225 --> 00:00:49.055
Excel, LibreOffice Calc, and Numbers open it directly.

00:00:49.055 --> 00:00:51.815
In Google Sheets, use File, Import, Upload.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:56.408
If you downloaded the file, open the workbook itself.

00:00:56.408 --> 00:00:58.073
Do not look for a website.

00:00:58.073 --> 00:01:00.018
The Start sheet is the index.

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:01.553
Read it before you type a number.

00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:05.281
Open W1 from lesson 0.3, and

00:01:05.281 --> 00:01:08.093
keep it from the first action.

00:01:08.093 --> 00:01:10.036
One line for every buy, sell,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.408
transfer, swap, fee, and income.

00:01:12.408 --> 00:01:14.413
The rest of the table is the map.

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:16.420
Match the sheet to the stage you are

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.210
in, not to the order of the tabs.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.284
Day one is W1, the records

00:01:21.284 --> 00:01:23.095
sheet, and you keep it.

00:01:23.095 --> 00:01:25.357
Before you use a protocol, open

00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:27.565
W3 and walk the six checks.

00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:29.507
While you hold a position, use the

00:01:29.507 --> 00:01:32.360
portfolio, the risk register, and the journal.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.140
Before you size the book up, write

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.575
the stress test and the incident playbook.

00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:38.481
When you run the bank, Modules

00:01:38.481 --> 00:01:40.202
12 through 14 fill the rest.

00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:42.845
A note can hold a number,

00:01:42.845 --> 00:01:44.797
and then that number goes stale.

00:01:44.797 --> 00:01:46.983
The health factor does not update, and

00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:49.132
the risk score is not multiplied.

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:51.367
The yellow cell is the one you type.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.682
The green cell is the course formula.

00:01:53.682 --> 00:01:56.562
And the credit policy on W8 reads the balance

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:59.442
sheet, so the check stays tied to the numbers.

00:02:00.742 --> 00:02:02.770
On Tools, yellow means you type,

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.159
and green means the sheet answers.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:09.841
The lesson 3.2 example is 10 units at $3,000,

00:02:09.841 --> 00:02:14.314
a threshold of 0.80, and $12,000 of debt.

00:02:14.314 --> 00:02:17.099
The health factor reads 2.00.

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:20.840
The liquidation price reads $1,500.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.039
Those figures are the lesson example,

00:02:23.039 --> 00:02:24.718
for learning, not a forecast.

00:02:26.018 --> 00:02:29.318
Here is the lesson 12.1 example, in order.

00:02:29.318 --> 00:02:33.079
Collateral of $300,000, plus a reserve

00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:36.658
of $40,000, is $340,000 of assets.

00:02:36.658 --> 00:02:38.548
Loans are $60,000.

00:02:38.548 --> 00:02:45.008
Equity is $340,000 minus $60,000, which is $280,000.

00:02:45.008 --> 00:02:47.532
LTV is $60,000 divided by

00:02:47.532 --> 00:02:50.648
the collateral, which is 20%.

00:02:50.648 --> 00:02:53.053
The health factor is 4.0, and

00:02:53.053 --> 00:02:55.938
the reserve covers about 7.6 months.

00:02:57.238 --> 00:03:01.463
On the balance sheet, equity reads $280,000.

00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:04.314
W8 reads that sheet and answers yes, because

00:03:04.314 --> 00:03:06.958
the health factor is above the floor.

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:11.529
The income sheet, in the lesson 13.3 example,

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:15.108
shows a payout of $16,310 a year.

00:03:15.108 --> 00:03:17.661
On the risk register, a score of 20 means

00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:20.213
do not hold it until the response is real.

00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:22.723
Question one.

00:03:22.723 --> 00:03:27.453
The lesson balance sheet has $300,000 of collateral,

00:03:27.453 --> 00:03:31.322
a $40,000 reserve, and $60,000 of loans.

00:03:31.322 --> 00:03:32.402
What is the equity?

00:03:36.822 --> 00:03:39.897
The answer: $280,000.

00:03:39.897 --> 00:03:42.452
Add the reserve, then subtract the loans.

00:03:42.452 --> 00:03:44.687
This is a lesson example, not your book.

00:03:45.987 --> 00:03:47.232
Question two.

00:03:47.232 --> 00:03:49.917
You have just finished lesson 0.3.

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:51.408
Which sheet do you open, and

00:03:51.408 --> 00:03:52.642
how long do you keep it?

00:03:57.062 --> 00:03:59.847
The answer: W1, the records sheet.

00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:01.952
One line per action, and you keep it.

00:04:03.252 --> 00:04:04.322
Your turn.

00:04:04.322 --> 00:04:07.027
Download the workbook and open the Start sheet.

00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:08.340
Find the lesson you are

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.952
on, and open that sheet.

00:04:09.952 --> 00:04:12.756
Replace one yellow example with a number of your

00:04:12.756 --> 00:04:15.287
own, and read what the green cell does.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:16.960
Never type a seed phrase,

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.312
a key, or a password.

00:04:19.612 --> 00:04:21.137
Three things to keep.

00:04:21.137 --> 00:04:24.092
The Start sheet tells you when each worksheet opens.

00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:25.549
Yellow is what you type,

00:04:25.549 --> 00:04:27.307
and green is the formula.

00:04:27.307 --> 00:04:29.557
And W1, the records sheet, stays

00:04:29.557 --> 00:04:31.397
open from the first action.

00:04:32.697 --> 00:04:34.262
Open the Start sheet.

00:04:34.262 --> 00:04:35.491
Then open the sheet for

00:04:35.491 --> 00:04:36.917
the lesson you are on.

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:39.055
The workbook is there to be filled in,

00:04:39.055 --> 00:04:41.247
beside the course, one lesson at a time.
